<title>USA: Tokheim to supply equipment in Mexico.</title>
<headline>Tokheim to supply equipment in Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WAYNE, Ind. 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokheim Corp said Monday it was selected by Monterrey, Mexico-based Empresas Amoxxo as a supplier of service station equipment for its Pemex gasoline franchisors.</p>
<p>Empresas Amoxxo is a joint venture between Amoco Corp's Amoco Oil Co and Fomento Economico Mexicano SA de CV. Its motorist service centers, with branded Oxxo Express convenience stores, will be operated in the same location with independently operated Pemex gasoline stations.</p>
<p>A total of 10 Oxxo Express service centers are expected to be open this year as part of an overall $250 million capital building porgram to be implemented in Mexico over the next 10 years.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
